WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Under a microscope, a slice of kidney is
dotted with tiny round knots of capillaries,

2
00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.290
each one in its own cup.

3
00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.490
Blood pressure pushes
fluid out of these knots.

4
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.570
Glucose, a sugar, goes straight through.

5
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.800
But blood cells and plasma
proteins stay behind in the blood.

6
00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:21.920
So what is this filter
actually built from?

7
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:26.090
In this mission, you'll zoom into
the wall between blood and filtrate,

8
00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.780
and find out what stops each thing.

9
00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:33.670
Then you'll read real kidney sections,
and use magnification to work out the true

10
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.690
size of what you see.

11
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.710
Your mission: work out what the
kidney's filter is built from.
